{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שור או כשב או עז", :translit "shor o kesev o ez", :gloss "an ox or a sheep or a goat"} {:he "בן נכר", :translit "ben neikhar", :gloss "son of a foreigner"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמיכות): our verse follows immediately after Lev 22:25, which discusses gentile offerings."}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 22:25 states that an animal with a blemish from a gentile may not be offered. Leviticus 22:27 opens the next verse with the list of animals eligible for sacrifice. The juxtaposition is read to restrict obligatory offerings specifically to Israelites, since the immediately preceding verse addressed voluntary gentile donations. The phrase 'ben neikhar' refers to a non-Israelite donor (Leviticus 22:25).", :sources ["Leviticus 22:25" "Leviticus 22:27"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והיה שבעת ימים וגו'", :translit "vehayah shiv'at yamim vagomer", :gloss "and it shall be seven days etc."}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Homiletic reading: the seven-day waiting period before offering a newborn animal (Lev 22:27) parallels the seven days of Creation. Slaughtering on any single day would appear to honor that day's creation rather than God Himself."}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 22:27 requires a newborn animal to remain with its mother for seven days before being offered. Genesis 1:1–2:3 describes six days of creation followed by God's rest on the seventh. The midrashic reading assigns each day of waiting to a creation: day one—heaven and earth (Genesis 1:1–5), day two—the firmament (Genesis 1:6–8), day three—sea and dry land (Genesis 1:9–13), day four—luminaries (Genesis 1:14–19), day five—creeping things (Genesis 1:20–23), day six—man (Genesis 1:26–31). Only after seven full days does the offering testify that God created everything and rested on the Sabbath.", :sources ["Leviticus 22:27" "Genesis 1:1–2:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (סמיכות): our verse follows immediately after Lev 22:25, which discusses gentile offerings.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Homiletic reading: the seven-day waiting period before offering a newborn animal (Lev 22:27) parallels the seven days of Creation. Slaughtering on any single day would appear to honor that day's creation rather than God Himself.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:00.535642081Z", :model "glm-5.2"}